# The repository root already ignores .env. This copy exists so the exclusion
# travels with the directory: these files are meant to be copied onto a server,
# where the root .gitignore is not present, and a self-hoster who keeps their
# deployment in their own git repository should not have to discover that rule
# for themselves.
#
# .env holds the JWT signing key, the OAuth client secret and the database
# password in plain text.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
